{"data": [{"author_id": "38254634", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:08:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118495806479093980"], "id": "2118495806479093980", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige For all the people who answer positively here: Have you ACTUALLY used this model? Please do so before you decide it’s great or not.", "url": "https://x.com/doth4580/status/2118495806479093980"}, {"author_id": "1669092639642210304", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:28:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118485537463975937"], "id": "2118485537463975937", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 19, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige Cool, but where is Qwen Flash Next on the charts? Why it is not included in v5?", "url": "https://x.com/ElhusseinFM/status/2118485537463975937"}, {"author_id": "1859673427524845570", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:56:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118477491090395359"], "id": "2118477491090395359", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 50, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige strong terminal use but weaker knowledge is a pretty honest tradeoff for a 33b", "url": "https://x.com/LightchainAI/status/2118477491090395359"}, {"author_id": "2011240577229377536", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:28:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118440422800601436"], "id": "2118440422800601436", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 69, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige Interesting placement. Heard that Nanbeige is pretty benchmaxxed and feels worse than Qwen across the board though.", "url": "https://x.com/DavidTranAI/status/2118440422800601436"}, {"author_id": "2036270919757471747", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:12:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118436225665433658"], "id": "2118436225665433658", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys how much of the extra output is retries after a tool error?\nthat's the bit i'd want separated before calling it thinking", "url": "https://x.com/mdp_sec/status/2118436225665433658"}, {"author_id": "2085027136025264128", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T19:28:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118425323746246799"], "id": "2118425323746246799", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@h1kz0r @ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige It's not an AA problem. Nanbeige always benchmaxed", "url": "https://x.com/liljomrh/status/2118425323746246799"}, {"author_id": "1561271873022877696", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T19:22:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118423630543527954"], "id": "2118423630543527954", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 46, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige if a 27b model achieves same as 33b model... it should be putted ahead of 33b one not behind.", "url": "https://x.com/1992Hikaro/status/2118423630543527954"}, {"author_id": "2114261495278391296", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T19:18:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118422699928440958"], "id": "2118422699928440958", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige Artificial Analysis 称，开放权重模型 Nanbeige4.3-33B 在 Intelligence Index v5 中得分 20，与 Qwen3.8 27B（xhigh）持平。", "url": "https://x.com/aixindongjing/status/2118422699928440958"}, {"author_id": "1437751191857999875", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T19:16:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118422217507922414"], "id": "2118422217507922414", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 76, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige If u actually tried this model you would know how trash it is across every single workload as compared to Qwen 3.8 27B.\nAA losing whatever credibility you still have left quick.", "url": "https://x.com/h1kz0r/status/2118422217507922414"}, {"author_id": "1663552685017268224", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:53:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118416414600274066"], "id": "2118416414600274066", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 58, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige same overall score as qwen3.8 27b but it declines 71% of questions and hallucinates less. apache 2.0 with a 524k window is a useful combo for running locally", "url": "https://x.com/DailyAIOfficial/status/2118416414600274066"}, {"author_id": "1891341713488388096", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:49:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118415415496073615"], "id": "2118415415496073615", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys Matching Qwen3.8 27B at 20 on your Intelligence Index at 33B is solid for an open Apache 2.0 model. Per your write-up, Nanbeige hits 30% on Terminal-Bench 4.0 versus 6% for Qwen3.8 27B, while trailing on knowledge. Agent work is where the dense mid-size models are separating.", "url": "https://x.com/thechrisgrey/status/2118415415496073615"}, {"author_id": "1613070948", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:42:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118413553778741391"], "id": "2118413553778741391", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 109, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige wow. Great launch @nanbeige team.", "url": "https://x.com/hebbarmp/status/2118413553778741391"}, {"author_id": "1988851885118484480", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:15:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118406924056379495"], "id": "2118406924056379495", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 146, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige 33B dense 能在笔记本本地跑，524K 上下文还挺能打的。终端使用强、知识弱这个取舍很实在，拿来当本地编程助手应该很顺手。", "url": "https://x.com/taiyanghere/status/2118406924056379495"}, {"author_id": "46498861", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:10:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118405576493593082"], "id": "2118405576493593082", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige Matching that score with a model small enough to run on a laptop changes who can experiment. The next gap is not intelligence, it is efficiency, and open weights are closing it fast.", "url": "https://x.com/raulnogales/status/2118405576493593082"}, {"author_id": "1466274357337014277", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:08:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118405022635716836"], "id": "2118405022635716836", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 80, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige 33B matching a 27B on AA Intelligence Index is mainly interesting for the terminal-use gap. Knowledge lagging while tool use leads usually tracks the post-train mix, not pretrain scale. Curious how it holds once tool schemas and longer trajectories are pinned.", "url": "https://x.com/flaviusburca/status/2118405022635716836"}, {"author_id": "417508671", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:02:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118403605548171551"], "id": "2118403605548171551", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 147, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige For terminal-heavy agents, that’s a particularly interesting tie", "url": "https://x.com/thesimaximalist/status/2118403605548171551"}, {"author_id": "870221240929140736", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:58:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118402688568217805"], "id": "2118402688568217805", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 69, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige Nanbeige is BOSS Zhipin's in-house foundation-model team; putting a 33B open release in the same AA Index band as Alibaba's Qwen3.8 27B is another China lab competing in that mid-size open-weights slot.", "url": "https://x.com/thePandaily/status/2118402688568217805"}, {"author_id": "1404099729525559301", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:58:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118402559354212840"], "id": "2118402559354212840", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 107, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige small enough for a laptop at what quant though? 33B dense at 4 bit is roughly 16.5GB of weights by my math, and that's before any KV cache for the 524K window. curious what context length the terminal bench runs actually used", "url": "https://x.com/Chahatusharma/status/2118402559354212840"}, {"author_id": "1857050273564282880", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:57:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118402250007589285"], "id": "2118402250007589285", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige I'd try the preserve_thinking switch part first. the model card says keep prior reasoning for multi-turn tool use and drop it for ordinary chat. Same weights, different context diet.", "url": "https://x.com/Adham__Khaled__/status/2118402250007589285"}, {"author_id": "2043452641208905728", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:53:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118401323129528389"], "id": "2118401323129528389", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 105, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige Interesting that terminal use is the bright spot. I wonder how long until Chinese open weights close the knowledge gap too?", "url": "https://x.com/TheGods_Eye/status/2118401323129528389"}, {"author_id": "1108548738065289221", "conversation_id": "2118400279788101824", "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:53:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118401319304118311"], "id": "2118401319304118311", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@ArtificialAnlys @nanbeige Another open model tying Qwen at 20 on the index. The leaderboard is becoming a group chat of 20s, ngl.", "url": "ht